  "Someone has presumably been attempting to repair some of the machinery in this room, because they left a drill lying around.",
  "This shiny cylindrical corridor is the connector between the Command Module, to the south, and the Scientific Sub-Module, to the north.",
  "This laboratory, which fills most of the middle level of the Sub-Module, is for the study of applications of the various space-related research that takes place on the other levels. Gangways lead up and down, and a door leads north. A connecting tube opens to the south.",
  "This is a small office associated with the lab to the south.",
  "This is the notebook of a certain Professor Schmidt, who was studying a strange pyramid discovered aboard a derelict alien ship and brought here.\n   Schmidt traced back the path of the alien ship; the path points out of the galaxy without nearing any star system. Further, extending the path leads straight to one of our smaller neighboring galaxies. Schmidt concludes that the ship and the pyramid are probably well over one billion years old!\n   Next, Schmidt studied the wall markings in the alien ship. A series of identical dots, they defied every computerized model of linguistic decipherment! Then, in an inspiration, Schmidt studied the dots for nonvisual properties. His diary vaguely refers to a breakthrough, saying, \"I guess my pal, the mayor, will get to show off his linguistic training.\"\n   Finally, Schmidt began concentrating his studies on the pyramid itself. He was able to discover very little, blaming this primarily on the unexplained failures of several crucial pieces of lab machinery.",
  "This laboratory conducts research into various space-related physical sciences. Gangways lead up and down, and there's a door to the north.",
  "Various biological sciences, as they relate to the environment of space, are studied in this laboratory. There is a gangway leading up, another leading down, and a door leading north.",
  "Lying on one of the desks is a scribbled note.",
